%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a8231245e4999eb498c6af83841371fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: QuesData 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  tests:
  - testsName: Test 3
    quesAnswers:
    - questions: What should you do when you hear an emergency vehicle approaching
        from behind with lights and sirens?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Stop immediately in the middle of the road
      - Slow down and continue
      - Stick to the right and clear the way
      - Move to the left lane
      answers: Stick to the right and clear the way
    - questions: What is the safest way to cross a traffic light intersection?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Speed up to avoid getting stuck at red
      - Slow down and always stop
      - Check the traffic and obey the traffic light
      - Honk before the intersection
      answers: Check the traffic and obey the traffic light
    - questions: What is the main reason for keeping a distance from the vehicle
        in front of you?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - To improve travel speed
      - To reduce fuel consumption
      - To ensure sufficient reaction time
      - To switch to another lane
      answers: To ensure sufficient reaction time
    - questions: What is the maximum speed on a rural road without built-up areas,
        if there are no other signs?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - 80 km/h
      - 110 km/h
      - 60 km/h
      - 90 km/h
      answers: 110 km/h
    - questions: In which cases is it permissible to cross a solid separation line?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - For overtaking
      - When the traffic light is green
      - For a left turn only
      - Always, if there is no oncoming traffic
      answers: For a left turn only
    - questions: How should you drive when you discover something is wrong with your
        vehicle while driving?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Slow down and continue cautiously
      - Stop immediately at the roadside
      - Turn on high beams
      - Honk and continue driving
      answers: Stop immediately at the roadside
    - questions: How should you drive when you are in an urban area and encounter
        a bus stop with passengers?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Stop to allow them to get on
      - Slow down and be ready to stop
      - Speed up and cross quickly
      - Drive in the left lane
      answers: Slow down and be ready to stop
    - questions: What does the sign "No U-Turn" mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Right turns are allowed
      - Left turns are prohibited
      - U-turns are prohibited
      - U-turns are allowed only with signaling
      answers: U-turns are prohibited
    - questions: What is the function of the tire pressure monitoring system?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - To reduce noise
      - To stabilize steering
      - To alert about low tire pressure
      - To balance vehicle braking
      answers: To alert about low tire pressure
    - questions: ' What is the correct way to drive on a wet and slippery road?'
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Slow down and avoid sharp maneuvers
      - Speed up to get out of the area
      - Stop at the side
      - Drive in the left lane
      answers: Slow down and avoid sharp maneuvers
    - questions: ' What is the correct way to drive when approaching an intersection
        with no signs?'
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Go first if there is no traffic
      - Yield to the vehicle on your right
      - Always stop
      - Speed up to avoid disruption
      answers: Yield to the vehicle on your right
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Overheight Cargo"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo is secured well
      - Prohibited for vehicles over the height limit
      - Allowed with additional vehicle escort
      - Allowed only during the day
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles over the height limit
    - questions: ' What is the correct way to drive when approaching a vehicle signaling
        to exit a parking space?'
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Speed up and pass in front of it
      - Stop and let it exit
      - Honk to warn
      - Pass in the opposite lane
      answers: Stop and let it exit
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Overlength Cargo"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo only extends from the back
      - Prohibited for vehicles with cargo exceeding the limit
      - Allowed with an escort vehicle
      - Allowed only at night
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with cargo exceeding the limit
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching a parked vehicle
        with emergency lights on?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Speed up and pass
      - Pass carefully and keep distance
      - Stop behind it
      - Pass in the opposite lane
      answers: Pass carefully and keep distance
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Overwidth Cargo"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo is marked with lights
      - Prohibited for vehicles with cargo wider than allowed
      - Allowed with an escort vehicle
      - Allowed only during the day
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with cargo wider than allowed
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching an intersection
        with the sign "Yield"?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Always stop
      - Slow down and continue if there is no traffic
      - Yield to the approaching vehicle
      - Go first if you are on the right
      answers: Yield to the approaching vehicle
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Hazardous Cargo"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo is secured
      - Prohibited for vehicles with hazardous cargo
      - Allowed with police escort
      - Allowed only during the day
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with hazardous cargo
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching a vehicle signaling
        to turn left at an intersection?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Overtake it from the right carefully
      - Overtake it from the left
      - Speed up and pass in front of it
      - Stop behind it
      answers: Overtake it from the right carefully
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Toxic Cargo" mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo is closed
      - Prohibited for vehicles with toxic cargo
      - Allowed with an escort vehicle
      - Allowed only at night
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with toxic cargo
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching a vehicle signaling
        to exit a parking space?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Speed up and pass in front of it
      - Stop and let it exit
      - Honk to warn
      - Pass in the opposite lane
      answers: Stop and let it exit
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles Over a Certain Weight"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Heavy vehicles are allowed if there are no additional signs
      - Prohibited for vehicles exceeding the weight limit
      - Allowed only for public vehicles
      - Allowed only at night
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles exceeding the weight limit
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching an intersection
        with the sign "One-Way Traffic"?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Drive only in the direction of the arrow
      - Allowed to drive in any direction
      - Allowed to turn left only
      - Allowed to turn right only
      answers: Drive only in the direction of the arrow
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Overweight Cargo"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo is secured well
      - Prohibited for vehicles with cargo exceeding the limit
      - Allowed if there is escort
      - Allowed only during the day
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with cargo exceeding the limit
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching a vehicle signaling
        to turn right?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Overtake it from the left carefully
      - Overtake it from the right
      - Speed up and pass in front of it
      - Stop behind it
      answers: Overtake it from the left carefully
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Flammable Cargo"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed for vehicles with flammable cargo if there is permission
      - Prohibited for vehicles with flammable cargo
      - Allowed with escort vehicle
      - Allowed only at night
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with flammable cargo
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching an intersection
        with the sign "Traffic Light Ahead"?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Slow down and prepare to stop
      - Speed up to make it
      - Stop immediately
      - Ignore the traffic light
      answers: Slow down and prepare to stop
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Explosive Cargo"
        mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo is secured
      - Prohibited for vehicles with explosive cargo
      - Allowed with police escort
      - Allowed only during the day
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with explosive cargo
    - questions: What is the correct way to drive when approaching a vehicle signaling
        to turn left at an intersection?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Overtake it from the right carefully
      - Overtake it from the left
      - Speed up and pass in front of it
      - Stop behind it
      answers: Overtake it from the right carefully
    - questions: What does the sign "No Entry for Vehicles with Toxic Cargo" mean?
      emogis: []
      options:
      - Allowed if the cargo is closed
      - Prohibited for vehicles with toxic cargo
      - Allowed with escort vehicle
      - Allowed only at night
      answers: Prohibited for vehicles with toxic cargo
